{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Good Leadership"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Becoming a Good Leader"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 6}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand actions, events, and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "the root of"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the main part of something, from which other things have developed "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Communication skills are at the root of effective management.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob01aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about managers. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "key skill"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an ability to do something that is necessary "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Being assertive is claimed to be a key skill for managers. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob01aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tactful"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not likely to upset or embarrass other people "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You ought to be tactful and communicate your ideas with confidence."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob01aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "execution"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a process in which you do something that has been carefully planned"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You should supervise the execution of it all and provide feedback. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob01aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "viewpoint"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a particular way of thinking about a subject"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is important to respect the other person's viewpoint."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob01aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to follow through"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to do what needs to be done to complete something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A manager should say what they are thinking and follow it through with actions. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob01aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "compensation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the \u200bcombination of \u200bmoney and other \u200bbenefits that an \u200bemployee \u200breceives for doing \u200btheir \u200bjob"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A good manager is known to consider each employee individually and match their strengths with their tasks and compensation.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob01aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to distribute"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to share things among a group of people, especially in a planned way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Putting all of this together involves creating strategies, and distributing tasks evenly. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob01aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to hesitate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to pause before saying something because you are nervous or not sure"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You will have to communicate your ideas without hesitating."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob01aud04"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le06ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Report Verbs with Impersonal Passive Constructions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When you want to avoid saying the generalized agent (<span class=\"italic\">they</span>, <span class=\"italic\">people</span>, <span class=\"italic\">everybody</span> etc.) of an action, you can use report verbs such as <span class=\"italic\">claim</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> mention</span>, <span class=\"italic\">request</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">point out </span>with a passive structure."}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can use the structure: <span class=\"italic\">it + passive reporting verb + that-clause</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Everybody knows that </span>my mother likes red wine. = </span> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">It is known that </span>my mother likes red wine.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The generalized agent (<span class=\"italic\">everybody</span>) and the active reporting verb (<span class=\"italic\">know</span>) are replaced by <span class=\"strong\">it </span>and a <span class=\"strong\">passive reporting verb</span> (<span class=\"italic\">known</span>)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at some other examples from the text:"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It is said that excellent communication skills are at the root of effective management.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Being assertive is claimed to be a key skill for managers. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "It is pointed out that excellent managers are open, friendly, and easy-going with with members of their team. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "It is presumed that the ability to connect with others is a vital skill. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "It is understood that being a good manager requires a lot of work. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Modals for Expressing Duty and Advice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use the modals should and ought to, to express your opinion about what's right or wrong. In a workplace scenario, you can use these modals to talk about a person's duties and responsibilities when it comes to the work at hand."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">ought to have</span> all your reports submitted by the end of the day, Friday. </span>(It's your duty) <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Mark <span class=\"strong\">should take </span>his responsibilities seriously</span>. (It's his duty) <br/> <span class=\"italic\">You really <span class=\"strong\">shouldn't e-mail </span>the boss until you're absolutely sure that's what you want to do. (Strong advice)</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The form of these structures is: <br/> subject + should/ought to + verb"}, {"type": "example", "content": "As a manager, your communication style ought to be clear and effective. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You should use the correct words to express your thoughts and encourage your staff to do the same."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You ought to be tactful."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Excellent managers should be open, friendly, and easy-going."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "In pairs, brainstorm a person who you both know that is a manager."}, {"type": "text", "content": "It could be a boss, teacher, or coach"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Using the six skills that make a good manager, for each category (communication style, assertiveness) give a score between 1 and 4.  (1 being the lowest and 4 being the highest)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your ranking with another group and explain your reasoning."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Then, using the six skills that make a good manager, assess whether or not you would be a good manager using the same process as before."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write an analysis of your strengths and your weaknesses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I collaborate with a partner"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I analyze an individual example and based on a scale assess their effectiveness as a manager."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I self-reflect and analyze my own strengths and weaknesses as a possible manager."}]}], "labs": [{"type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "exercises": [{"type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express claiming, mentioning, requesting, or pointing out an idea, thing,  or issue in the workplace environment."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express duty and advice related to work and job issues."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about how to become a good leader."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What do you think makes someone a good manager or leader?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What kind of skills and characteristics should they possess? "}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type