"title": "", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"images": [{"time": "", "image": "engenn11le06ob01re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn11le06ob01re2img01.jpg", "text": "Qualities of a Good Manager\n</br></br>There are six skills that are crucial for anyone who manages projects and people. Five of the six are people skills. People skills are about being able to communicate effectively with people in a friendly way.</br>As a manager, your communication style ought to be clear and effective. You should use the correct words to express your thoughts and encourage your staff to do the same. It is said that excellent communication skills are at the root of effective management.", "id": 1}, {"time": "26500", "image": "engenn11le06ob01re2img02.jpg", "text": "Being assertive is claimed to be a key skill for managers. You ought to be tactful and communicate your ideas with confidence and without hesitating, all while respecting the other person's viewpoint.</br>It is presumed that the ability to connect with others and build a level of trust is another vital skill. Excellent managers should be open, friendly, and easy-going with others, especially with members of their team. They ought to take an interest in others and interact in an informal, relaxed manner making it enjoyable for others to work with them.", "id": 2}, {"time": "56500", "image": "engenn11le06ob01re2img03.jpg", "text": "It is all about building a trustworthy relationship. A manager should say what they are thinking and follow it through with actions. A good manager is known to consider each employee individually and match their strengths with their tasks and compensation.</br>A big part of a manager's role is like putting together a puzzle. It is assumed that the puzzle pieces are employees, tasks, goals and data. Putting all of this together involves creating strategies, distributing tasks, supervising the execution of it all and providing feedback.</br>Judging by the six qualities, it is understood that being a good manager requires a lot of work.", "id": 3}], "audiosrc": "engenn11le06ob01re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le06ob01re2img01.jpg"}}], "id": 1}]}]}